
A lisp interpreter that is desgined to be the brain of an AI agent in a neuro-symbolic cognitive architecture
or as called today "harness"

the llm writes code into the REPL and the REPL influnces the context of the agent, with event based hooks,
builtin mcp tools and helpers that get called with PTC

the llm is the programmer and bespoke person, the runtime is the program, and the steerer of the llm

you can think of this agent as having 2 sides of the brain:

- llm which is the creative, inspired, encoding tacit knowledge
- lisp runtime which is the logical, deterministic, experince driven, memory holding part of the brain

they both write to each other

- [x] basic lisp interpreter
- [x] setup tests, commitlint
- [x] setup pi for testing the setup in cli
- [ ] mcp intergraion with:
    - [ ] load_mcp: (e.g. `(load-mcp "linear")`) which loades the tools as symboles, 
    the become a real binding in the interpreter's global environment (e.g. `(linear/list-issues :query "x")`)
    - [ ] helpers such as: list-mcps, list-tools, search-tools (which uses a search api on docs and names of tools)
- [ ] setup a web client for the agent
- [ ] add a vizualization tool that goes from the lisp script into a 3d force graph
- [ ] add memory and hooks macros and helpers

this repo contains:

- lisp interpreter
- pi coding agent extension

later it will include:

